      "content": "okay but i actually think i had a booster like 4 or 5 years ago... i'm pretty sure. and honestly it's not even throbbing or anything, it's just a small little hole. if i use a lot of the peroxide to basically kill everything in there and then keep it covered with a bandage, that should be fine right? i really don't want to spend $200 just for a tetanus shot i probably don't even need. can't i just monitor it for a few days to see if it gets bad before i commit to going in?",
